{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261116T082131Z_dev-04_flat_a2e1", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "For the 4b on-shell cascade, the fixed-r comparison shows the AMS-02 antiproton limits approaching or intersecting the GCE-preferred regions at the smaller mass ratios r = 0.2–0.4. At the larger ratios shown (r up to 1.0, i.e. r ≈ 0.5–1.0 in the 0.2–1.0 grid), the antiproton limits stay above the GCE-preferred regions, so they do not constrain them there. The paper says this relative strength depends on the cascade spectra and the adopted cosmic-ray propagation model (BIG).", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "6.3"}]}, "turns": 7, "seconds": 20.667, "tool_calls": 6, "tool_result_chars": 345600, "input_tokens": 16, "output_tokens": 778, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 87192, "cache_read_input_tokens": 653912, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-16T08:21:52+00:00"}
